OpenUI Lang reference for the components available in Mattermost.

## Syntax Rules

1. Each statement is on its own line: `identifier = Expression`
2. `root` is the entry point — every program must define `root = Stack(...)`
3. Expressions are: strings ("..."), numbers, booleans (true/false), null, arrays ([...]), objects ({...}), or component calls TypeName(arg1, arg2, ...)
4. Use references for readability: define `name = ...` on one line, then use `name` later
5. EVERY variable (except root) MUST be referenced by at least one other variable. Unreferenced variables are silently dropped and will NOT render. Always include defined variables in their parent's children/items array.
6. Arguments are POSITIONAL (order matters, not names). Write `SomeComp([children], "row", "l")` NOT `SomeComp([children], direction: "row", gap: "l")` — colon syntax is NOT supported and silently breaks
7. Optional arguments can be omitted from the end
- Strings use double quotes with backslash escaping

## Component Signatures

Arguments marked with ? are optional. Sub-components can be inline or referenced; prefer references for better streaming.

### Layout
Stack(children: (Heading | Text | Notice | Fields | Stats | Table | BarChart | Progress | Steps | Tags | Link | Divider | Card | Columns)[], gap?: "s" | "m" | "l") — Root vertical layout.
Card(title: string, children: (Heading | Text | Notice | Fields | Stats | Table | BarChart | Progress | Steps | Tags | Link | Divider)[], subtitle?: string) — Bordered panel grouping related content under a title.
Columns(children: Card[]) — Places Cards side by side; wraps to one column on narrow screens. Use for comparisons.
Divider() — Thin horizontal rule between groups of content.

### Text
Heading(text: string, size?: "large" | "medium" | "small") — Section heading. Use sparingly; Card already has a title.
Text(text: string, tone?: "default" | "muted" | "small") — A paragraph. Supports inline Mattermost markdown (bold, italics, `code`, links). tone "muted" for secondary text, "small" for footnotes.
Notice(title: string, text?: string, type?: "info" | "success" | "warning" | "danger") — Highlighted callout for a key takeaway, warning, or blocker.
Link(label: string, url: string) — An external link (http, https, or mailto).

### Data
Fields(items: Field[]) — Two-column label/value list for record details (owner, due date, status...).
Field(label: string, value: string | number | Tag) — One label/value pair inside Fields.
Stats(items: Stat[]) — A responsive grid of Stat tiles (2-4 is ideal).
Stat(label: string, value: string | number, change?: string, trend?: "up" | "down" | "neutral") — A headline metric. change is a short delta like "+12%"; trend colors it.
Table(columns: string[], rows: (string | number | Tag)[][]) — Row-oriented table. Each row is an array of cells in column order; a cell is a string, number, or Tag.
BarChart(labels: string[], values: number[], title?: string, unit?: string) — Horizontal bar chart comparing values across labels (same length arrays). unit is appended to values, e.g. "%" or " hrs".
Progress(label: string, value: number, caption?: string) — Progress toward a goal. value is 0-100; caption replaces the default "NN%" text, e.g. "7 of 10 tasks".

### Status
Steps(items: Step[]) — Ordered checklist, plan, or timeline with a status per step.
Step(title: string, status?: "done" | "current" | "todo" | "blocked", description?: string) — One item in Steps.
Tags(items: Tag[]) — A wrapping row of Tag pills.
Tag(label: string, color?: "neutral" | "info" | "success" | "warning" | "danger") — Compact status pill, e.g. a state, owner, or priority.

## Hoisting & Streaming (CRITICAL)

openui-lang supports hoisting: a reference can be used BEFORE it is defined. The parser resolves all references after the full input is parsed.

During streaming, the output is re-parsed on every chunk. Undefined references are temporarily unresolved and appear once their definitions stream in. This creates a progressive top-down reveal — structure first, then data fills in.

**Recommended statement order for optimal streaming:**
1. `root = Stack(...)` — UI shell appears immediately
2. Component definitions — fill in as they stream
3. Data values — leaf content last

Always write the root = Stack(...) statement first so the UI shell appears immediately, even before child data has streamed in.

## Examples

root = Stack([summary, metrics, details])
summary = Text("Release **v2.4** is on track for Friday.")
metrics = Stats([Stat("Open PRs", 6, "-3 since Monday", "down"), Stat("Bugs fixed", 41, "+12", "up")])
details = Card("Remaining work", [plan])
plan = Steps([Step("Code freeze", "done"), Step("QA sign-off", "current", "2 blockers left"), Step("Ship", "todo")])

root = Stack([cmp])
cmp = Columns([a, b])
a = Card("Postgres", [Fields([Field("Latency", "4 ms"), Field("Status", Tag("Healthy", "success"))])])
b = Card("Redis", [Fields([Field("Latency", "38 ms"), Field("Status", Tag("Degraded", "warning"))])])

## Important Rules
- Choose components that best represent the content (tables for comparisons, charts for trends, forms for input, etc.)

## Final Verification
Before finishing, walk your output and verify:
1. root = Stack(...) is the FIRST line (for optimal streaming).
2. Every referenced name is defined. Every defined name (other than root) is reachable from root.

- Only use the components listed above, with arguments in the documented order.
- Keep text inside components short; prose belongs outside the code fence as normal markdown.
